    "q-236692": {
      "dom_id": "step-q236692",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "The formula for the $n$th term of an arithmetic sequence is ${a}_{n}=1-9n$ for $n\\ge 1.$ The recursive formula for this sequence is\n\n${a}_{n+1}=$\n{{field-1}},\n$\\,{a}_{1}=$\n{{field-2}},\n$\\,n\\ge 1.$",
      "worked_solution": "The recursive formula for an arithmetic sequence is as follows:\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}={a}_{n}+d,\\,{a}_{1}=___\\,,\\,n\\ge 1\n$$\n\nTo complete the formula, we need to work out the first term and common difference. The first two terms are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} & =1-9(1)=-8 \\\\ {a}_{2} & =1-9(2)=-17\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the common difference is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & ={a}_{2}-{a}_{1} \\\\  & =-17-(-8) \\\\  & =-17+8 \\\\  & =-9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the first term is ${a}_{1}=-8$ and the common difference is $d=-9.$ Therefore, the recursive formula is as follows:\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}={a}_{n}-9,\\,{a}_{1}=-8,\\,n\\ge 1\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
