    "q-45058": {
      "dom_id": "step-q45058",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "What is the explicit formula for the $n$th term of the arithmetic sequence\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}={a}_{n}-3,\\,\\,{a}_{1}=7,\\,\\,n\\ge 1?\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "The explicit formula for the $n$th term of an arithmetic sequence is\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}={a}_{1}+(n-1)d,\\,n\\ge 1,\n$$\n\nso we need to determine the first term ${a}_{1}$ and the common difference $d.$\n\nWe are given that the first term is ${a}_{1}=7,$ and we can use the recursive rule to compute the second term, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{2} & ={a}_{1}-3 \\\\  & =7-3 \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the first and second terms, we can compute the common difference:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & ={a}_{2}-{a}_{1} \\\\  & =4-7 \\\\  & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we substitute ${a}_{1}=7$ and $d=-3$ into the formula for the $n$th term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}+(n-1)d \\\\  & =7+(n-1)(-3) \\\\  & =7-3n+3 \\\\  & =-3n+10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the formula for the $n$th term is\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=-3n+10,\\,n\\ge 1.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
